Subject: [PATCH] Android: give the standard library's compiles a versioned triple

The NDK's `sys/cdefs.h` refuses to compile against an unversioned Android
triple:

    error: Unversioned target triples are not supported!
      #if !defined(__ANDROID_MIN_SDK_VERSION__)

The minimum SDK version that header derives from the triple is what gates every
availability declaration in the sysroot, so the compiler has to be told which
API level it is building for. Swift already knows: `swift_get_host_triple`
supplies `SWIFT_ANDROID_API_LEVEL` through `get_target_triple`, which is why
every C and C++ target links against `aarch64-unknown-linux-android24`.

The standard library's own Swift compiles do not go that way. Their flags take
the Darwin branch when the SDK is a Darwin platform and otherwise fall through
to the raw, unversioned SDK triple, so `stdlib/public/Platform` is compiled as
`aarch64-unknown-linux-android` and the Android SDK build fails as soon as the
NDK is new enough to enforce this.

Supply the API level on that branch. It does not belong in the SDK triple
itself: `get_versioned_target_triple` composes versioned triples by appending to
it, so versioning it there yields `android2424` for every C and C++ target, and
module files are named by their triple even though a Swift module built for one
API level is loadable by any other.

Sentinel: NUCLEUS_SWIFT_ANDROID_VERSIONED_TRIPLE

diff --git a/stdlib/cmake/modules/SwiftSource.cmake b/stdlib/cmake/modules/SwiftSource.cmake
index 55a00bf01c3..16b284a2c72 100644
--- a/stdlib/cmake/modules/SwiftSource.cmake
+++ b/stdlib/cmake/modules/SwiftSource.cmake
@@ -274,4 +274,17 @@ function(_add_target_variant_swift_compile_flags
   else()
-    list(APPEND result
-        "-target" "${SWIFT_SDK_${sdk}_ARCH_${arch}_TRIPLE}")
+    # NUCLEUS_SWIFT_ANDROID_VERSIONED_TRIPLE: the NDK's `sys/cdefs.h` refuses to
+    # compile against an unversioned Android triple, because the minimum SDK
+    # version it derives from the triple gates every availability declaration in
+    # the sysroot. Darwin above supplies its deployment version through
+    # `get_target_triple`, and `swift_get_host_triple` already supplies the API
+    # level the same way for Android; only the standard library's own compiles
+    # reached this branch and dropped it. Append it here rather than in the SDK
+    # triple, which would double the version for every caller that composes a
+    # versioned triple from it, and would version module file names that are
+    # deliberately API-level agnostic.
+    set(target "${SWIFT_SDK_${sdk}_ARCH_${arch}_TRIPLE}")
+    if("${sdk}" STREQUAL "ANDROID")
+      set(target "${target}${SWIFT_ANDROID_API_LEVEL}")
+    endif()
+    list(APPEND result "-target" "${target}")
   endif()
